    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0497" n="481" xml:id="pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.00/2–949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-09T17:00:00-03:00">February 9, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>145. Usually reliable source reports Perón stalked out of meeting of government
                    officials yesterday threatening resign and has not appeared at office today.
                    Perón known to be greatly worried financial-economic situation. Two well-known
                    local persons also called on me today stating Bramuglia, Ares,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d301-f1"/> and Gomez Morales,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d301-f2"/> all
                    threatening resign, ground existing financial economic chaos. Embassy has heard
                    such rumors many times recently, but in view report from usually dependable
                    source believed Department should be informed. We think little likelihood Perón
                    resigning, but situation is tense and administration deeply concerned over
                    present situation. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d301-f1" n="1" xml:id="d301-f1-content">
                <p>Roberto Ares, Argentine Minister of Economy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d301-f2" n="2" xml:id="d301-f2-content">
                <p>Alfredo Gómez Morales, Argentine Minister of Finance and President of the Central
                    Bank.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
